        },
        {
          "question": "What is the OpenFlow logical switch?",
          "answer": "An OpenFlow logical switch is an abstraction consisting of flow tables, group table, meter table, and OpenFlow channel, which may be implemented as a virtual switch, a physical switch, or a portion of a physical switch with a specific set of ports"
        },
        {
          "question": "What is SDN network slicing?",
