        {
          "question": "How does the competitive exclusion principle shape community structure?",
          "answer": "The competitive exclusion principle states that two species competing for the same limiting resource cannot stably coexist, meaning species must differentiate their niches to reduce competition and persist together, driving ecological specialization, resource partitioning, and ultimately influencing biodiversity patterns within communities"
        },
        
