      "context": "The UNI ISO/IEC 27001 standard is an international standard that defines the requirements for an information security management system (ISMS). It is designed to help organizations protect their information systematically and consistently through the adoption of a risk-based process. The standard is based on the PDCA (Plan-Do-Check-Act) cycle and includes organizational, technical, and physical measures. ISO 27001 requires risk assessment, implementation of security controls, and continuous review and improvement of the system. The main purpose is to ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of information.",
